      "description": "Inspect or change the Workbench working location without changing PiG's session cwd. Use {} for status, {path} for a local directory, or {reset:true} to return to the origin. Relative paths use the captured location. A change waits at most 2 seconds for active mutations and persists before activation.",
      "promptSnippet": "Inspect or change the working location for coding tools."
    },
    {
      "name": "edit",
      "label": "edit",
      "description": "Edit local UTF-8 files using either {hashline} tagged batches from read output, or {path, edits:[{oldText,newText}]} exact replacements. Tagged batches start with [path#TAG] copied from read. Use PUT 2.=2: (replace line 2), PUT 2.=5: (range), PUT \u003e5: (insert after), PUT \u003c1: (BOF), PUT \u003e$: (EOF), or PUT 6*: (structural block); each literal payload row starts with +. edit.mode restricts the accepted branch: hashline, replace, or auto (both); there is never automatic fallback after a rejected patch. CUT, REM, MV and registers are supported. All coordinates refer to the original snapshot; block anchors require syntax evidence. Seen-line guards cover complete consumed ranges. Exact replacements must be unique and non-overlapping. Every resource is preflighted before writes, then locked and revision-checked immediately before atomic replacement. A partial I/O failure reports landed and unattempted effects; there is no rollback. Changed sources are relocated only when anchors are unambiguous; otherwise reread the current source.",
      "promptSnippet": "Apply tagged original-coordinate edits or unique exact-text replacements."
    },
    {
      "name": "find",
      "label": "find",
      "description": "Walk a local directory or registered provider root for file names matching a glob pattern. Links and noWalk subtrees are not followed, control files and .git are skipped, local .gitignore rules and exclusions apply, and bounds report complete:false.",
      "promptSnippet": "Find files by name glob under a directory."
    },
    {
      "name": "grep",
      "label": "grep",
      "description": "Search file contents at a local path or registered provider file/directory. Line selectors are accepted only for explicit files. Pass exactly one regex pattern, or literal patterns for an OR search (literal:true). Relative paths resolve against the Workbench location. Local traversal honors nested .gitignore rules; explicitly named file roots remain searchable. Binary, oversized and incomplete provider files are skipped and listed in Details; hitting a bound reports complete:false instead of pretending the results are exhaustive.",
      "promptSnippet": "Search file contents with exact matches and honest limits."
    },
    {
