      "description": "Inspect or control a session-owned shell job. action=list needs no id; status/output/wait/kill/write/eof require id. output uses a monotonic byte cursor; evicted bytes are reported. wait is cancellable without killing a background job; kill terminates its process group. write sends exact text and eof closes stdin.",
      "promptSnippet": "Inspect, await, stop or send input to owned jobs."
